      {
        "_uid": "59649c77-fea7-f1ec-2eb3-1152f4640a8d",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Professor Brenda Leibowitz (1957-2018)",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr. Leibowitz was the South African Research Chair Initiative (SARChI)'s Chair for Teaching and Learning in Post-secondary Education and Training. At the University of Johannesburg, she was a Professor in the Faculty of Education as well as the Chair of Teaching and Learning. She was also the convener for several prestigious programmes including the Teaching Advancement at University (TAU) Fellowships Programme and the South African Universities Learning and Teaching (SAULT) Forum. She was also on the editorial board of the International Journal for Academic Development (IJAD) of which she had previously been a co-editor. She held a PhD in Education from the University of Sheffield. Her research interests included the scholarship of teaching and learning, social justice, practice based approaches to learning and professional learning.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
